From: Ely Office
Subject: LOK: Writer appends paragraphs after the body, the cursor kept

- .uno:ElyAppendParagraphs (Text, Style) adds Text's lines as paragraphs
  after the body's last paragraph (or after a table or section ending it),
  in one undo step, without moving any view's cursor or selection.
- Style is a paragraph style's programmatic name, empty for Standard;
  pool styles not yet in the document are made. Each new paragraph takes
  the style alone: the last paragraph's direct formats and list are not
  carried over.
- The slot sits on SwBaseShell, so a selected frame or image does not hide
  it. An unknown style leaves the document as it was.

